    "gas_EF_kg_per_kWh": "IPCC 2006 Guidelines Vol. 2 Table 2.2, 56,100 kg CO2/TJ NCV -> 0.182 kg/kWh GCV, direct combustion (same scope as the APA grid factor)",
    "eta_lorenz_sensitivity": "0.45-0.52: Carnot efficiencies implied by DEA HTHP sheets (COP 2.05 at 100 K lift); 0.63: Andersen et al. (2024) polynomial for the HTHP unit (upper envelope, extrapolated: source below 0 °C and isothermal)",
    "co2_price_scenario": "EUA Dec contract 82.40 EUR/t on 5 Oct 2026 (S&P Global Commodity Insights)",
    "chiller_cop": "Sinnott and Towler (2020), Chemical Engineering Design, 6th ed. (Elsevier, ISBN 978-0-08-102599-4), Sec. 6.4.4, Eq. 6.20: real COP about 0.6 x Carnot for a simple cycle. Evaporator at cold utility -1 °C minus 5 K (refrigerated-brine approach 3-5 K, Sec. 12.7.3), condenser at ambient 15 °C + 10 K cooling-water rise + 5 K approach = 30 °C: 0.6 x 267.15/36 = 4.45. Check: CoolProp ammonia cycle (Andersen et al. 2024 assumptions, sink 15->25 °C) gives 4.52. Padullés et al. (2026) give no chiller credit"
